{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"documentation_gaps": {}, "duration_s": 7527.4, "landed_paths": 0, "missing_artifacts": 0, "next": "fresh observation in a new domain per STATE.md named next action", "outcome": "worked", "push_requested": false, "summary": "Completed E144: View-count principle on WordPress plugins. Fresh observation in a previously untouched domain (wordpress.org plugin directory). Experiment tested whether need-related plugins have systematically higher active installation activity than random plugins using the view-count principle protocol (E071/E072 precedent). Key result: Negative — need-related plugins have 13.8 pp LOWER active installation rate than random plugins (82.5% vs 96.3%, z = -3.29, p = 0.05), opposite of the principle's prediction. All experiment files created: PROTOCOL.md, collect.py, results.json. This adds to the mission's body of evidence that the view-count principle, while supported on 5 domains with metadata (PyPI, NPM, NuGet, Discourse forums, Stack Exchange non-software), does not produce candidates in any tested domain and the 'candidate_seat_empty' boundary condition is reinforced. Next action: choose a fresh observation domain per D083, continuing the systematic domain sweep.", "unlogged_changes": 20}, "host": "instance-20260717-0947", "kind": "session_end", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 28, "session": "2026-10-15-003-design-and-run-a-fresh-observation-exper", "ts": "2026-10-15T11:32:56+00:00"}
